● <adaptive_rules>
  - streets.sim lines must follow `[Startknoten]-->[Endknoten]:[Länge]m,[Art]x,[Limit]max` with no
  spaces; [Art] is 1 or 2
  - During `load` the network must be validated for completeness, correctness and adherence to all
  value ranges
  - File paths passed to `load` must not contain spaces
  - Loading requires three input files in one folder: streets.sim, crossings.sim, cars.sim
  - The program must use the provided SimulationFileLoader class to read the files
  - The program must be able to simulate several hundred cars
  - When filling a street at load the first car is placed at the end; subsequent cars follow with 10
   m spacing
  - cars.sim lines must follow `[ID],[Straße],[v],[a]` with no spaces
  - Cars placed on a street at load must respect a minimum distance of 10 m between cars
  - crossings.sim lines must follow `[ID]:[Dauer]t` where Dauer==0 indicates roundabout and Dauer>0
  indicates crossing
  - Errors from SimulationFileLoader must be handled sensibly (e.g., shown as an error message)
  - Initial green phase for all crossings is 0 (first connected street has green)
  - A valid network may contain no cars; a network with no nodes, streets, and cars can still be
  valid
  - Street length must be integer in [10,10000] meters and max speed integer in [5,40] m/Tick
  - At initialization cars start with speed 0 m/Tick and desired direction 0
  - Invalid commands (incorrect keyword or parameters) must produce an error message printed to the
  command line.
  - `simulate` must error if ticks is invalid or negative or if called before the first successful
  load
  - Crossing green-phase duration (for Dauer>0) must be integer in [3,10] Ticks
  - Street nodes may have up to four incoming and four outgoing streets and must have at least one
  incoming and one outgoing street
  - `position` must error for unknown ID or if called before the first successful load
  - Assignment submission is automatically scored zero if any of the mandatory rules listed in the
  document are violated.
  - Mandatory tests must be passed before other tests are evaluated.
  - Pass the path string directly to the SimulationFileLoader constructor; the path string itself
  need not be validated
  - Car desired speed must be integer in [20,40] m/Tick and acceleration integer in [1,10] m/Tick²
  - Error messages must be a single line and contain no line breaks.
