  - A valid command always consists of a keyword and optionally a space-separated parameter.
  - The Javadoc author tag must contain only the student's u-Kürzel.
  - During `load` the network must be validated for completeness, correctness and adherence to all
  value ranges
  - File paths passed to `load` must not contain spaces
  - Loading requires three input files in one folder: streets.sim, crossings.sim, cars.sim
  - The program must use the provided SimulationFileLoader class to read the files
  - Placeholders in square brackets like [path] are never part of the actual program output.
  - Initial green phase for all crossings is 0 (first connected street has green)
  - Crossing green-phase duration (for Dauer>0) must be integer in [3,10] Ticks
  - A valid network may contain no cars; a network with no nodes, streets, and cars can still be
  valid
  - At initialization cars start with speed 0 m/Tick and desired direction 0
